{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Pethora.</b> Like מצרימה (to Egypt); to Pethor." "<b>Land of his people.</b> They are Arameans, and so 'of Pethor, Aram Naharaim.' And in the derash: 'Balaam' = 'he swallowed' (בלע), for this one is an Aramean. And if on account of Beor his father — behold, he is a son of Ahasuerus before Ahasuerus; only they are two." "<b>Which is on the river.</b> Meaning Aram Naharaim." "<b>Eye of the land.</b> I have explained it."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:51.374311286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}